Randomness from Nebula (docs/w4.md W4d). WTF's random device opens
/dev/urandom on a Unix and stops the process when it cannot; Kosmos has no
device files, and a process asks the kernel for entropy (SYS_ENTROPY),
which arc4random_buf does and cannot fail at. So Kosmos takes Fuchsia's
shape: no descriptor held, and each request filled by the system's call.
JavaScriptCore asks for it the moment a VM is made, to salt its hashes.

